                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "SWITCH"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_tokens": 32000,
                        "p": 0.25
                      },
                      "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
                      "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
                      "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
                      "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
                    },
                    "errorNodeId": "1765961014063",
                    "name": "Text Format"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1765961345304"
                  },
                  "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_TEXT_FORMAT",
                  "id": "1765961317206",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1765961317209_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Transform eligible monetary values and dates in each `content` string. Return only the final valid JSON object with the same structure, without reasoning, explanation, or markdown.\n\nContent : {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LOOP_SUMMARY_ITEMS.$currentItem}}\n\nApply these rules in order. An earlier rule takes precedence.\n\n1. Protect\n\n* Treat each existing `{date:...}` or `{amount:...,currency:...}` as one atomic formatter token. Do not parse, normalize, nest, or format it again.\n* Use surrounding language and token boundaries to identify each complete business entity name or identifier span, including request, file, integration, invoice, document, and reference names or codes.\n* Preserve each such span exactly, even when a component resembles a date, amount, or currency. Never format a substring within it or within a mixed alphanumeric token. Underscores and hyphens may be identifier characters; separators alone do not establish value meaning.\n* Protect only the entity or identifier span; independent values elsewhere remain eligible.\n* Preserve existing HTML tags and their attributes.\n\n2. Classify\n\n* Outside protected spans, format only a whole candidate that context and token boundaries unambiguously identify as an actual value. If uncertain, leave it unchanged.\n* A monetary value requires both a standalone amount and an explicit currency indicator: either a currency code or a standard currency symbol. Do not format an amount without a currency indicator or a currency indicator without an amount.\n* Never interpret a value with a `%` sign, including a decimal percentage, as monetary.\n* A date or date reference requires a complete, valid, unambiguous day, month, and year. Do not format a month alone, year alone, or month and year.\n\n3. Transform\n\n* Replace an eligible monetary value with the literal token `{amount:<value>,currency:<CODE>}`. Convert a currency symbol to its ISO currency code. In `<value>`, omit the currency symbol and digit-group separators while preserving the sign and decimal precision.\n* Replace an eligible date with the literal token `{date:<YYYY-MM-DD>}`.\n* Apply any supplied `formatHints` strictly.\n* If a hint requests bold formatting, wrap only the complete formatted amount or date token with `<B>...</B>`, at most once.\n\n4. Preserve and output\n\n* Apart from required token replacement and hint markup, preserve all text, punctuation, sentences, HTML, JSON properties, and structure. Do not add or remove sentences or introduce data. Keep `sequence` unchanged.\n* Silently verify these rules and valid JSON, then output only the JSON object.\n"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"sequence\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"content\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n        },\n        \"type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "errorNodeId": "1765961014063",
                    "name": "Text Format Code",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "const input = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LOOP_SUMMARY_ITEMS.FIN_AP_LLM_TEXT_FORMAT.$output\n\nlet inputText = input.content.join(\" \");\nif(inputText.startsWith('[') && inputText.endsWith(']')){\ninputText = inputText.slice(1,-1)\n}\n\n\nvar output = {\n  type: input.type,\n  sequence: input.sequence,\n  content: inputText\n};\n\nreturn output;"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1765961201966"
                  },
                  "code": "FIN_AP_CODE_TEXT_FORMAT_CODE",
                  "id": "1765961345304",
                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
                  "type": "CODE"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
